From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Nov 2026 13:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: let the tc police flow reach the PPE meter

With airoha_ppe_meter=1 no tc police action is accepted, whatever the
rate, burst or conform/exceed actions are.  Two separate checks stand in
the way, and the first of them fires before the meter is even looked at.

1. airoha_ppe_meter_validate() refuses a non-zero police->mtu.  That
   field is never zero here: tc leaves the limit unset and act_police
   fills it in itself (either ~0 or the rate-table cell size, whichever
   applies) before the action is stored, so the test rejects every
   police action tc can build.  tc even reports the value it handed
   over: "police ... rate 10Mbit burst 32Kb mtu 2Kb action drop".  The
   meter group sizes its bucket from rate and burst only, so an mtu has
   nothing to land on; stop using it as a gate and keep the avrate and
   overhead refusals.

2. data.eth was filled from the ETH_ADDRS dissector key inside
   "case 0:" only, i.e. only for addr_type 0 (a plain L2 flow).  For an
   IPv4/IPv6 tuple the MACs stayed zero even when the user matched
   src_mac/dst_mac, and the validity test further down then refused the
   flow with -EINVAL.  Every FOE entry this driver writes carries the
   address pair of the frame the PPE has to build, so an IP flow needs
   those MACs just as much as an L2 one: read the key whenever
   cls_flower registered it, and keep the "L2 needs it" test in case 0.

Nothing else changes: with airoha_ppe_meter=0 police is still refused
in the POLICE arm, and a flow without src_mac/dst_mac is still refused.

Tested on XR1710G (AN7581, 7.4-rc3): before this, every combination of
src_mac/dst_mac, conform-exceed and action returned EOPNOTSUPP; the
mtu value handed over by tc was read back with "tc -s -d action show".

Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -379,9 +379,15 @@
 				   "packet-rate police is not supported");
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
-	if (police->avrate || police->overhead || police->mtu) {
+	/* tcfp_mtu is never zero: act_police replaces an unset limit with the
+	 * rate-table cell size before the action is stored, so testing it here
+	 * says nothing about what the user asked for and refuses every police
+	 * action tc can build.  The meter group sizes its bucket from rate and
+	 * burst alone, so there is nothing an mtu could change either.
+	 */
+	if (police->avrate || police->overhead) {
 		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_MOD(extack,
-				   "avrate/overhead/mtu police is not supported");
+				   "avrate/overhead police is not supported");
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	}
 	/* The PPE group carries one token rate and the probe leaves the
@@ -2550,18 +2556,25 @@
 	has_ports = flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_PORTS);
 	use_3t = !has_ports && airoha_ppe_3t;
 
+	/* Every entry this driver writes carries the address pair of the frame
+	 * the PPE has to build, so the rule has to hand the MACs over whatever
+	 * the tuple is.  cls_flower registers the eth-addrs key only when the
+	 * user matched src_mac/dst_mac, hence the key test rather than
+	 * addr_type; a plain L2 flow still cannot do without them.
+	 */
+	if (flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_ETH_ADDRS)) {
+		struct flow_match_eth_addrs match;
+
+		flow_rule_match_eth_addrs(rule, &match);
+		memcpy(data.eth.h_dest, match.key->dst, ETH_ALEN);
+		memcpy(data.eth.h_source, match.key->src, ETH_ALEN);
+	}
+
 	switch (addr_type) {
 	case 0:
 		offload_type = PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE;
-		if (flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_ETH_ADDRS)) {
-			struct flow_match_eth_addrs match;
-
-			flow_rule_match_eth_addrs(rule, &match);
-			memcpy(data.eth.h_dest, match.key->dst, ETH_ALEN);
-			memcpy(data.eth.h_source, match.key->src, ETH_ALEN);
-		} else {
+		if (!flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_ETH_ADDRS))
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
-		}
 		break;
 	case FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV4_ADDRS:
 		offload_type = use_3t ? PPE_PKT_TYPE_IPV4_ROUTE :
